
# OpenTelemetry OTLP log export (opt-in). Standard OTel variable names — read by the SDK
# itself, not by our code. Leave OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT empty to opt out: with no
# endpoint, chassis/otel_logging.py (or utils/otel_logging.py) never imports opentelemetry
# and never sends a byte over the network; the local logging.FileHandler is unaffected.
# ⚠️ MEASURED 2026-09: the Python Logs signal is "Development" status upstream (Traces/Metrics
# are Stable) — see chassis/otel_logging.py's module docstring for the source and the
# fire-and-forget rationale that follows from it.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
# Defaults to "unknown_service" upstream when left blank; name it after the project.
OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=
# Comma-separated key=value pairs, e.g. "authorization=Bearer <token>". Never commit a real
# value here — this file ships as .env.example too.
# ⚠️ SET THIS AND THE ENDPOINT MUST BE https:// (or loopback). These headers are how a
# provider's API key is carried, and OTLP/HTTP sends them in cleartext over http:// —
# otel_logging.py REFUSES to start the exporter in that case and warns, rather than leaking
# the credential to anything on the path.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=
# Both variables above have signal-specific forms — OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_ENDPOINT and
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_LOGS_HEADERS — which OVERRIDE the generic ones for logs. Set one of
# those instead if logs go somewhere other than traces/metrics; otel_logging.py honours the
# same precedence the SDK does.
